            <div xml:id="d653">

                <pb facs="0777" n="1611" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1611"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 654.119/189</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Sharp</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-04-25T19:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 25, 1918, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3710. For McFadden [from
                    War Trade Board]:</p>
                <p>No. 49. Embassy’s 3660, April 19, noon. Your 41. We will act in concert with
                    other Governments represented on Contingent Commission and will adopt the plan
                    suggested in your cable by virtue of which we will hereafter, in all cases where
                    it appears that unauthorized exports from Switzerland to Central Powers have
                    taken place, withhold exports of corresponding raw materials to Switzerland
                    until receipt from Swiss Government of satisfactory explanation and of an
                    assurance for the future.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
